// Title: HackTool - Hydra Password Bruteforce Execution
// Sigma ID: d5911c4f-e2c5-4a67-a72e-6d37a18a7060
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Vasiliy Burov
// Date: 2020-10-05 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1110, T1110.001
// Description: Detects command line parameters used by Hydra password guessing hack tool
// False positives:
//   - Software that uses the caret encased keywords PASS and USER in its command line
// References:
//   - https://github.com/vanhauser-thc/thc-hydra
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/7490edb4783550895f8ac7b1ff297eaa8fda0d2a/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_hydra.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "-u " and ProcessCommandLine contains "-p ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "^USER^" or ProcessCommandLine contains "^PASS^")
